index 000000000..91478ca67
--- /dev/null
+++ b/hertzbeat-alerter/LIFECYCLE_OUTBOX.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Native alert lifecycle outbox
+
+Enable using `lme.lifecycle.enabled=true`, configured `source-node`, `admission-url`
+ending in `/v1/logs`, and an owner-only `token-file`. HTTPS uses the JVM trust store
+and hostname verification; isolated loopback HTTP supports a local Serve hop.
+Redirects are rejected. Tokens and receiver/content/label fields are never exported.
+
+Schema-only initialization creates `hzb_lifecycle_outbox` and
+`hzb_lifecycle_quota` through the two common entity definitions, then seeds quota
+row `(1,0)`. Missing initialization fails admission. Normal startup must use schema
+validation, not DDL updates.
+
+Automatic persisted single/group status transitions, manual status edits/deletes,
+silence/inhibition/repeat suppression, and notification selection enter the outbox
+in the same application database transaction as their corresponding persisted
+state. Suppressed alerts are persisted. A quota row lock serializes enabled state
+admission across workers/processes. Queue capacity defaults to 64 MiB of immutable
+payload; individual events are at most 8 KiB. Full admission rolls back state.
+
+Notification work starts after transaction commit. Its queued/rejected/handler
+completion/failure observations have separate transactions. Handler completion does
+not establish that a receiver received a notification. Alert group timers and the
+upstream calculation/reduction caches remain in memory; this outbox guarantees
+committed database transitions, not recovery of calculations before admission.
+
+The sender retries immutable batches of at most 64 events with bounded 1–60 second
+backoff. Its five-second HTTP exchange has a 4 KiB response bound. Only HTTP 202
+with `ack=local_fsync` and an exact inserted/replayed count permits a transactional
+handoff. Crashes or bad receipts retain the original events. Local-fsync transfers
+custody to the log delivery spool; destination transport and readback verification
+remain that spool's independent obligations. No event is marked sink-verified here.
+
+Verification: 40 focused tests passed on the pinned checkout using JDK 25 and Maven,
+including real Spring/H2 rollback, reconnect, quota exhaustion, false HTTP receipts,
+and stable replay through a synthetic loopback HTTP endpoint. The run used
+`-pl hertzbeat-alerter -am` and selected `LifecycleOutboxContractTest`,
+`LifecycleProjectionContractTest`, `DbAlertStoreHandlerImplTest`,
+`AlertNoticeDispatchTest`, `AlarmSilenceReduceTest`, `AlarmInhibitReduceTest`,
+`AlarmGroupReduceTest`, and `AlertServiceTest`, with
+`-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false`. This is local source verification,
+not deployment or destination readback acceptance.
